# Project Reflection

This project helped me understand how Power BI can be used to build a structured and version-controlled business intelligence solution. 
I created a star schema by separating the sales data into a fact table and dimension tables for date, city, product, and store format. 
This helped me understand how relationships between tables affect filtering and analysis.

I also learned how Git and GitHub can be used to track changes in a BI project. 
Making separate commits for different stages made the development process easier to follow and provided a clear history of the work completed.

GitHub Copilot was useful when developing the DAX measures. 
I reviewed the suggestions instead of using them directly. 
For example, the initial Month-over-Month growth suggestion needed to be corrected because the current month should use the existing filter context rather than shifting the date forward.
I also reviewed and adapted the suggestions for the running total, city ranking, and AOV measures.

The final dashboard provides an overview of total sales, monthly sales trends, and differences in sales performance between cities. Overall, this project improved my understanding of Power BI data modeling, DAX, dashboard development, Git, GitHub, and Copilot-assisted development.
